    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1.6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVEg">IV Eg</ref> 1.6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.6" corresp="#wit-f">Ðonne wille ic, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þás Godes gerihta standan æghwær gelice on minum anwealde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.6" corresp="#wit-c">Ðonne wille ic, þæt ðas Godes gerihta standan ægðer gelice on minum anwealde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1.6" corresp="#wit-q">Uolo ętiam, ut hoc decretum stabile ác firmum in omnibus locis dominationis nostrę perseueret.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="1.6" corresp="#wit-c">Ðonne wille ic, þæt ðas Godes gerihta standan æghwær gelice on minum anwealde;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-c">Further, it is my will that these ecclesiastical dues be everywhere alike throughout my dominion.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Ferner will ich, dass diese Kirchen-Gerechtsame überall in meinem Gebiete gleichmässig gelten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Further I will that these dues of God stand equally everywhere in my dominion.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
